  "observations": [
    "The coordinating agent inspected all seven final art-a2 images: the original reference, High front/three-quarter/underside/head detail, Balanced front and Economy front.",
    "Closed organic lofts remove the earlier board-like flipper and tail appearance, and the white fan/pinch at the nose is no longer visible in the inspected views.",
    "The material reads as polished yellow gold. Six faceted emerald eyes sit in gold settings, with seated lower-jaw curves and facial detail.",
    "All three figures retain the recognizable original support silhouette at High, Balanced and Economy; the lower tiers do not drop a figure or the overall stand shape.",
    "All five successful browser-a2 screenshots were inspected by the coordinating agent. The gold stand fits beneath the existing globe and retains three figures at every tier; the High RU preview and Balanced/Economy screenshots show unobstructed controls.",
    "At 390 px the outer stand rings are clipped by the existing viewport, without page overflow or blocked controls. The reloaded 1440 px view restores the stand and map, but captures a transparent header during its fade-in; it is not evidence of fully settled navigation appearance."
  ],
  "remainingVisibleIssues": [
    "The result is still a stylized sculptural ornament, not photorealistic animal anatomy or final fulfillment of the user's realism requirement.",
    "The unchanged globe lighting still creates strong violet accents and reflections on the gold; no global lighting change is claimed.",
    "All six small emerald eyes are present; their gemstone identity and facets read better in close-up and remain limited at normal phone scale.",
    "Earlier library, wood-identity, metal-response and uniform-paper realism issues remain open in the preserved surface review."
  ],
